// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna — runtime-spawn blacklist.
//
// Entities that vanilla's RUNTIME spawner (the continuous one that places things near players) may
// never spawn. WORLDGEN IS UNAFFECTED: these still generate with new chunks exactly as their mods
// intend. Only the near-player spawning is stopped.
//
// Both entries are things Cycle of Life deliberately does NOT manage, which is precisely why they
// need this: with nothing else governing them, vanilla spawns them unchecked, and in practice that
// meant far too many of them turning up around players.
//
// Patterns are matched against the full "domain:path" entity code. Delete a line to hand that
// spawning back to vanilla. Other packs can add their own "noRuntimeSpawn" lists; all are combined.
{
  "noRuntimeSpawn": [

    // DRACONIS NESTS (17 codes: both dragons, the wyvern, and the drake in all fourteen rock colours).
    // Nests are chain seeds - the nest -> egg -> dragon chain is the mod's own, so the simulation only
    // observes them. The design assumed a seed's spawn conditions cap themselves. These do not: the
    // drake nest rolls at 0.00003 across fourteen colours, and the wyvern nest's cap is written
    // "draconis:draconis:wyvern-nest-{type}", a doubled domain that matches no entity, so it limits
    // nothing. It is the NESTS that spawn at runtime, not the eggs - in Draconis 1.5.0 every egg has a
    // runtime chance of 0.0. Blocked here, Draconis populations come from worldgen nests and the eggs
    // those nests lay, which is how the mod grows them in any case.
    "draconis:*-nest-*",

    // FotSA CARCASSES (12 codes across Bovinae, Caninae, Capreolinae, Casuariidae, Machairodontinae and
    // Pantherinae). Ambient carrion placed as set dressing, with live runtime chances of 0.00001 to
    // 0.0001. Already excluded from the simulation, since a corpse has no ecology to model; this stops
    // them accumulating around players.
    "*carcass*"
  ]
}
